    "text": "Is the following analogue of the Cayley–Hamilton theorem true for the free\ngroup Fn of rank n: If w ∈ Fn and φ ∈ Aut Fn are such that ⟨w, φ(w), . . . , φn (w)⟩ =\nFn , then ⟨w, φ(w), . . . , φn−1 (w)⟩ = Fn ?                     O. V. Bogopolski",
